# Findings

Every number below is generated by `python -m cf.report && python -m cf.render` from the results
files of commit `{{ n.commit }}`; `bash reproduce.sh` regenerates them from the raw data. Each claim
states its evidence and what it is compared against. References this work does not produce: the
species labels of the Zenodo records (cryo 13890874; room temperature 15062310, 15062327, 15062343),
the paper (Thompson et al., Acta Cryst. D 81, 278-290, 2025, doi:10.1107/S2059798325004589) and DIALS's
own reference test data (the paper's cosym coordinates and labels shipped in DIALS's tests). The
definitions of "found", "false group", draws and detection limit were fixed in `PREREGISTRATION.md`
before any trial was scored; its amendments say what had been seen when each was written.
"k90" is the smallest minority size k found in at least 90% of draws at that and every larger size
tested, also given as the fraction k / (majority + k); intervals are exact 95% (Clopper-Pearson) over
draws.

