## F5. Counting noise of DIALS's pairwise correlations

The same crystals measured in disjoint wedge segments give repeat measurements of every pairwise
correlation. Observed repeat scatter of the single-population residuals over the scatter each noise
model predicts (1 = calibrated; cryo, `cf/noisecal.py`):

{{ noise_table(n, C) }}

The bootstrap over reflections overstates the noise up to five-fold where pairs share few reflections
(median 9 shared reflections per pair at 0.3 degrees); measurement errors alone (redrawn from sigma)
understate it up to seven-fold; the large-sample error of Fisher's z with DIALS's effective number of
reflections is within a factor 0.56-1.43, and is what {{ P }} uses. The last column is the same check for
correlations of amplitudes (Pearson's r of the square roots of the intensities over the shared
reflections, the matrix F6 compares with DIALS's): Fisher's z with the number of shared reflections
understates their noise by up to 1.7-fold.
