## F9. A defect of today's DIALS: names shifted when cosym drops a data set

`CorrelationMatrix` filters data sets with too few reflections before cosym, but cosym filters again
after the partiality and I/sigma cuts and can drop one more. OPTICS's labels then follow cosym's rows,
while DIALS names the members of each cluster by position in its full list of data sets
(`_prep_optics_for_info`), so every data set after the dropped one is named as its predecessor. In
{{ dc.affected }} of {{ dc.n_trials }} room-temperature trials (all at 1 degree per crystal) cosym dropped a crystal; in
{{ dc.dropped_last }} of them it was the last in DIALS's list, where the shift changes no name; in {{ dc.names_shifted }} the names are
shifted (the dropped crystal is reported as an outlier and the last crystal not at all). Every number
above takes today's output as DIALS reports it; the proposed change works on cosym's rows and inherits
the naming. The fix (name cluster members through cosym's lattice ids) is outside the change proposed
here.
{%- endif %}

